	"data": "Intelligent Forgetting for a Personal Knowledge Vault\n\nThe vault has 8,200+ markdown files, 10,425 wikilinks, and no pruning mechanism. It accumulates without bound. This note explores what intelligent forgetting would look like — grounded in biology, existing systems, and practical vault architecture.\n\nWhy Forgetting Matters — The Biological Case\n\nForgetting is not a bug. It's the most underappreciated feature of biological memory. A system that remembers everything is an archive, not a mind.…",
